From f79552be77959b1a2eabeb5d1fc0a567e3ef342c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herbert Marselas <marselas@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:25:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] device-libs: extended_bit_ops, subgroup
 shuffle/shuffle_relative/rotate, extended_types

- cl_khr_extended_bit_ops: bitfield_insert, bitfield_extract_signed/unsigned,
  bit_reverse for every integer scalar and vector type.
- cl_khr_subgroup_shuffle / _shuffle_relative / _rotate: ds_bpermute with the
  lane index kept inside the wave; rotate is mod the max sub-group size,
  clustered rotate within aligned power-of-two clusters.
- cl_khr_subgroup_extended_types: 8/16-bit broadcast/reduce/scan (32-bit
  arithmetic; add truncates, min/max clamp so a promoted exclusive-scan
  identity becomes the narrow type's) and vector broadcast for every type.

These are also what the SPIR-V translator lowers OpBitField*/OpBitReverse
and OpGroupNonUniformShuffle*/RotateKHR to.
---
 .../opencl/src/integer/extbitops.cl           | 43 ++++++++++
 amd/device-libs/opencl/src/subgroup/subext.cl | 48 +++++++++++
 .../opencl/src/subgroup/subshuffle.cl         | 86 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 177 insertions(+)
